    assignment: "Take a small piece of Java code with deliberately inconsistent naming (mix camelCase, PascalCase, and snake_case for different variables/methods within the SAME file) and rewrite it to follow consistent, standard Java conventions throughout.",
    goingDeeper: "Automated formatters (like `google-java-format` or the formatter built into most IDEs, configured with a shared team style file) remove coding-standard debates from code review entirely - rather than a human reviewer commenting 'please use camelCase here,' the formatter simply enforces it automatically on save or as a CI check, freeing actual human code review time to focus on logic, design, and correctness instead of surface-level formatting nitpicks.",
