    goingDeeper: "Rust's most commonly auto-implemented traits via `#[derive(...)]` include `Debug` (for {:?} formatting, mentioned in the Structs lesson), `Clone` (for the explicit .clone() deep-copy method from the Ownership lesson), and `PartialEq` (for == comparison) - deriving these automatically for your own structs, rather than hand-writing each implementation, is genuinely idiomatic, common Rust practice for straightforward cases.",
