    goingDeeper: "Once your mini-project's core works, try adding a custom error type (an enum implementing the standard `std::error::Error` trait, rather than a plain String) for its Result's Err variant - this is the genuinely idiomatic, production-grade way real Rust libraries represent their own specific failure modes, letting callers match on distinct error VARIANTS rather than just comparing error message strings.",
