    prerequisites: [],
    concept: "Kotlin was created by JetBrains (the company behind IntelliJ IDEA) and became Android's OFFICIALLY PREFERRED language in 2019 (Google's own announcement), specifically because it fixes several genuine, longstanding pain points in Java (this course's own Java path) - dramatically less boilerplate for common patterns, and NULL SAFETY built directly into the type system (covered in depth in a dedicated lesson later in this path) eliminating Java's infamous `NullPointerException` as a compile-time-preventable category of bug rather than a runtime surprise.\n\nKotlin compiles to the SAME JVM bytecode Java does, and is 100% INTEROPERABLE with existing Java code in both directions - a Kotlin file can call Java classes directly, and a Java file can call Kotlin classes directly, with zero friction. This is a genuinely deliberate design choice: it meant (and still means) that any existing Java codebase, including Android's own enormous existing ecosystem, could adopt Kotlin gradually, file by file, rather than requiring an all-or-nothing rewrite.\n\nIf you've studied this course's Java path already, expect Kotlin to feel like 'Java, but with the verbosity and a whole category of null-related bugs surgically removed' - most core concepts (classes, interfaces, the JVM's underlying execution model) transfer directly, while the SYNTAX and specific safety features are where Kotlin genuinely innovates.",
