    goingDeeper: "Aggregate functions genuinely only make full sense when combined with `GROUP BY` (covered in the next module) for computing PER-GROUP summaries (like 'average GPA per department') rather than one single summary across the ENTIRE table - this lesson's plain, ungrouped aggregate queries are really just the special case where the whole table is treated as a single group, a connection worth keeping in mind heading into the GROUP BY lesson.",
